# Frontend (React + Vite + Tailwind)

## Code

- TypeScript, functional components and hooks only.
- Styling with Tailwind utility classes; no CSS modules or styled-components.
- Organize by feature: `src/features/<domain>/` (components, hooks, api calls), shared UI in `src/components/`.
- Component and variable names in English; UI text in Spanish.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
export function ProductList({ products }: ProductListProps) {
  return <h2 className="text-lg font-semibold">Productos</h2>;
}
```

## API

- Base URL from `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL`; never hardcode it.
- All HTTP calls go through a single API client in `src/lib/api.ts` (handles JSON, auth token, errors).
- Format money with `Intl.NumberFormat('es-AR', { style: 'currency', currency: 'ARS' })`. Treat amounts from the API as strings (Decimal), don't do float math for totals shown as final.

## GitHub Pages constraints

- Static hosting only: no server-side code, no secrets in the frontend bundle.
- Set `base` in `vite.config.ts` to the repo name (e.g. `/facturador_ferreteria_gaston/`).
- Use `HashRouter` (or a 404.html fallback) so page refreshes don't 404.

## Render free tier

- The API sleeps after inactivity and the first request can take ~30-50 s. Always show a loading state and a clear "conectando con el servidor..." message instead of failing silently.
- Disable submit buttons while a request is in flight to avoid duplicate sales.
